From 7fe12afc41a8557fc6c0196b97612d4d161c2b20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 223/229] panvk: PANVK_DEBUG=mem driver memory accounting and
 report

Rationale: Fallout 4 on the G615 (build 110) held 2.6 GiB of kbase memory
while DXVK accounted for 1.6 GiB; the other ~1 GiB could not be split
between tiler heaps, BC raw stores and pools without a counter
(worklogs/g615-dxvk/fo4-memory-analysis-2026-10-23.md, fix 1).

Every private BO is counted under a kind (device pools, shaders, command
buffer CS / descriptor / TLS slabs, device TLS, descriptor pools, BC raw
stores, u_trace, other pools, misc), with current bytes, peak and count.
Pool slabs are classified by the pool label (panvk_priv_bo_create_pool),
other callers pass the kind (panvk_priv_bo_create_kind); both are
line-neutral edits so later series hunks keep their offsets. The kbase
tiler heap contexts (alive, peak, bytes committed at HEAP_INIT, renewals,
synchronous TERMs, TERM backlog peak), BC raw store events (spills,
read-backs, pins, skipped lazy reads) and VkDeviceMemory are reported too,
with VmRSS / RssAnon / RssFile / VmSwap and MemAvailable.

logd is stopped on some phones, so the line goes to PANVK_MEM_LOG=<path>
(appended, "%p" = pid) when set, else to mesa_logi (MESA_LOG_FILE works).
At most one line per PANVK_MEM_LOG_MS (default 10000) from the CSF submit
path, plus a "panvk-mem-final" line at queue destroy.

Knob: PANVK_DEBUG=mem or PANVK_MEM_LOG=<path> (off by default; the
counters are a few atomics per BO create/destroy). Arch: counters in shared
code (all), report from the CSF queue (v10+).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
